; selfie.cs.uni-salzburg.at

; Abstraction for bitr's product of rotor's RISC-R model of the binary
; tests/cellfie-test.r with cellfie's cell rule on the layout
; tests/cellfie-test.rle, see cellfie.md and make product. Its states are
; the states of the two models by name. Its output step holds when the
; token is on the path of an instruction cell, about to execute it: that
; is where a RISC-R instruction begins, and where rotor's model takes a
; step. Its bad states are where the two differ then: the pc, a register,
; or one of the two memory words, which are the first two words of the
; data segment at 0x11000 and the memory cells in column 14 of rows 5
; and 4 of the grid of 16x8 cells; and the token must be on the path
; with nothing in transit. Written by hand for the hand-laid layout.

1 sort bitvec 1 ; Boolean, and the address of a word in the data segment
2 sort bitvec 64 ; word
3 sort bitvec 5 ; register
4 sort array 3 2 ; register file
5 sort array 1 2 ; data segment of two words
6 sort bitvec 4 ; column
7 sort bitvec 3 ; row
8 sort bitvec 7 ; cell index: row, column
9 sort bitvec 8 ; cell: kind, orientation, mirror
10 sort array 8 9 ; cells
11 sort array 8 2 ; cell words
12 sort bitvec 2 ; heading

; rotor's model

20 state 2 core-0-pc
21 state 4 core-0-initialized-register-file
22 state 5 core-0-loaded-data-segment

; cellfie's model

30 state 6 token-x
31 state 7 token-y
32 state 12 token-heading
33 state 2 token-pc
34 state 2 token-address
35 state 2 token-data
36 state 4 token-registers
37 state 10 cell-kinds
38 state 11 cell-words

; step: the cell under the token is an instruction cell, kind 4, and the
; token is heading where the cell is oriented

40 concat 8 31 30 ; cell index
41 read 9 37 40 ; cell
42 slice 7 41 2 0 ; kind
43 constd 7 4 ; instruction
44 eq 1 42 43
45 slice 12 41 4 3 ; orientation
46 eq 1 32 45
47 and 1 44 46
48 output 47 step ; a RISC-R instruction begins

; nothing is in transit

50 zero 2
51 neq 1 34 50
52 neq 1 35 50
53 or 1 51 52
54 and 1 47 53
55 bad 54 token-in-transit ; address or datum of the token is not zero on the path

; pc

60 neq 1 20 33
61 and 1 47 60
62 bad 61 pc-differs ; pc of the token is not the pc of the machine

; memory: 0x11000 is cell (14,5), 0x11008 is cell (14,4)

70 zero 1
71 one 1
72 constd 8 94 ; 5 * 16 + 14
73 constd 8 78 ; 4 * 16 + 14
74 read 2 22 70
75 read 2 38 72
76 neq 1 74 75
77 and 1 47 76
78 bad 77 word-at-0x11000-differs
79 read 2 22 71
80 read 2 38 73
81 neq 1 79 80
82 and 1 47 81
83 bad 82 word-at-0x11008-differs

; registers

100 constd 3 0
101 read 2 21 100
102 read 2 36 100
103 neq 1 101 102
104 and 1 47 103
105 bad 104 register-zero-differs

110 constd 3 1
111 read 2 21 110
112 read 2 36 110
113 neq 1 111 112
114 and 1 47 113
115 bad 114 register-ra-differs

120 constd 3 2
121 read 2 21 120
122 read 2 36 120
123 neq 1 121 122
124 and 1 47 123
125 bad 124 register-sp-differs

130 constd 3 3
131 read 2 21 130
132 read 2 36 130
133 neq 1 131 132
134 and 1 47 133
135 bad 134 register-gp-differs

